# Personal Finance Tracker — Flask Web App

Convert the existing PostgreSQL schema ([personal_finance_tracker_project.sql](personal_finance_tracker_project.sql)) into a production-ready Flask web application with modern UI, multi-user auth, and full financial tracking capabilities.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Google OAuth Setup**: You'll need to create a Google Cloud project and configure OAuth 2.0 credentials (Client ID + Client Secret). I'll provide instructions during the auth phase, but you'll need a Google account with access to the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Open Exchange Rates API Key**: You'll need to sign up for a free account at [Open Exchange Rates](https://openexchangerates.org/signup/free) to get an App ID for live currency conversion. The free tier provides 1,000 requests/month.

> [!WARNING]
> **PostgreSQL Service**: Your PostgreSQL 18 service failed to start (permissions error). Before we begin, you'll need to fix this — likely by running the service start command as Administrator. I'll help troubleshoot this in Phase 1.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Gmail SMTP**: For email notifications, you'll need to generate a Gmail App Password (requires 2FA enabled on your Google account). Regular Gmail passwords won't work with SMTP.

