### Phase 4: Core Business Logic (Services Layer)

Port all stored procedures and functions to Python with improvements:

#### [NEW] [services/balance.py](finance_app/app/services/balance.py)
- `get_balance(account_id)` — replaces `get_balance()` SQL function
- `deposit(account_id, amount, description)` — replaces `deposit_amount()` procedure
- `withdraw(account_id, amount, description)` — replaces `withdraw_amount()` procedure
- **Improvement**: Add validation (account ownership, active status), atomic transactions, and audit logging

#### [NEW] [services/transfer.py](finance_app/app/services/transfer.py)
- `fund_transfer(from_id, to_id, amount, notes)` — replaces `fund_transfer()` procedure
- **Improvement**: Support cross-currency transfers with exchange rate locking

#### [NEW] [services/budget.py](finance_app/app/services/budget.py)
- `check_budget(user_id, category_id, month)` — check if spending exceeds budget
- `send_overspend_alert(user_id, budget)` — trigger email notification
- **Improvement**: Configurable alert threshold (default 80%), prevent duplicate alerts

#### [NEW] [services/savings.py](finance_app/app/services/savings.py)
- `get_goal_progress(goal_id)` — replaces `get_goal_progress()` SQL function
- `contribute_to_goal(goal_id, amount, account_id)` — add money from an account to a goal
- `update_goal_status(goal_id)` — replaces `update_goal_status()` procedure
- **Improvement**: Track individual contributions, auto-complete goal when target reached

#### [NEW] [services/currency.py](finance_app/app/services/currency.py)
- `fetch_exchange_rates()` — call Open Exchange Rates API, cache in DB
- `convert(amount, from_currency, to_currency)` — convert using cached rates
- `get_supported_currencies()` — list available currencies
- **Improvement**: Cache rates in `exchange_rates` table, refresh at most once per hour

#### [NEW] [services/notifications.py](finance_app/app/services/notifications.py)
- `send_budget_alert(user, budget, spent_amount)` — send email via Flask-Mail
- `check_recurring_dues(user_id)` — find due recurring transactions
- **Improvement**: Store notification history in DB for in-app review

#### [NEW] [services/audit.py](finance_app/app/services/audit.py)
- `log_action(table, operation, record_id, user_id, old_value, new_value)` — unified audit logger
- **Improvement**: Capture before/after JSON diffs for all changes

